s://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H43SYY631S0Z8YR/prj_1K7HK8Q4S1S0D4W4/pjd_1KVAA1X881S0Q1CZ/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"Project Design Document | 17 Jun 2026\"},{\"h\":\"/ghg-entry/rmv_1KYD9KRCD1S02J7Q?tab=calculation-view\",\"t\":\"See GHG entry →\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H43SYY631S0Z8YR/prj_1K7HK8Q4S1S0D4W4/pjd_1M1FC57011S0RNY8/verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H43SYY631S0Z8YR/prj_1K7HK8Q4S1S0D4W4/pjd_1M1FC4PRQ1S0HC6Y/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H43SYY631S0Z8YR/prj_1K7HK8Q4S1S0D4W4/pjd_1KVBSZVB01S0XHP2/validation_and_verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H43SYY631S0Z8YR/prj_1K7HK8Q4S1S0D4W4/pjd_1KVBBX6RT1S0A41A/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H43SYY631S0Z8YR/prj_1K7HK8Q4S1S0D4W4/pjd_1KVAA1X881S0Q1CZ/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nBICRS\\n1,000Y+\\nTIRE Project\\nVaulted Deep\\nISSUED\\n2,774.85\\nBUFFER POOL\\n55.936\\nCREDITING PERIOD\\n03 Jan 2026 to 03 Jan 2031\\nSummary\\nRemoval method\\nCalculation overview\\nFeedstocks\\nProject documentation\\nCertificates\\nReversal risk\\nSummary\\n\\nVaulted deploys slurry injection technology to geologically sequester organic wastes for the purpose of permanent carbon removal. The TIRE facility is a biosolids injection well co-located with the City of LA's Terminal Island wastewater treatment plant. Over the course of its operations over ten years, the site has safely and effectively injected more than 450,000 tons of biosolids. Vaulted has waived fees for waste volumes over the 5-year baseline to enable the city to send additional volumes to the site. Vaulted only credits those volumes over the baseline.\\n\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nCurrent verifier\\n350Solutions\\n->\\nProject code\\nB9B1\\nApproval date\\n17 Jun 2026\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiomass Geological Storage v1.1\\nAccreditation\\nSUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT GOALS\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nTIRE Project\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nProject Design Document\\n17 Jun 2026\\nCalculation overview\\nCalculations demonstrating 2.07 tCO₂e removed from TIRE Project on 09 Jul 2026\\nSee GHG entry →\\nNet CO₂e Removed\\n2.070 tCO₂e\\nSequestrations\\n2.217 tCO₂e\\n-\\nActivities\\n148 kgCO₂e\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nView full screen\\nFeedstocks\\n\\nFeedstocks are the validated input materials that have been used for this project.\\n\\nName\\tCategory\\tValidated\\nLACity_Biosolids\\tBiomass\\t17 Jun 2026\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n01 Sep 2026\\tVerification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n01 Sep 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n17 Jun 2026\\tValidation and Verification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n17 Jun 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n17 Jun 2026\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 5 of 6\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nCertificates\\nIssued\\n2,774.85\\nRetired\\n0\\nBuffer pool\\n55.936\\nCrediting period\\n03 Jan 2026 to 03 Jan 2031\\nIssuances\\nRetirements\\nIssue date\\tIssued\\tBuffer pool\\tSupplier allocation\\n01 Sep 2026\\t2,347.33\\t47.285\\t2,300.045\\n17 Jun 2026\\t427.52\\t8.651\\t418.869\\nShowing 2 of 2\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nReversal risk\\n\\nThe risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 2% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to Vaulted Deep's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 55.936 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 1,465.017 certificates.\\n\\nVaulted Deep has no reversals to date.\\n\\nLearn more about reversal risk\"}"